          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which of the following features of schizophrenia is classified as a negative symptom?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Persecutory delusions</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Delusions are positive symptoms — they represent experiences added to the patient's mental life that are absent in healthy individuals.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Affective flattening</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Affective flattening is one of the '5 As' of negative symptoms (avolition, alogia, anhedonia, affective flattening, asociality), representing a loss or diminution of normal emotional expression.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Third-person auditory hallucinations</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Auditory hallucinations are positive symptoms. They are among the most common psychotic features in schizophrenia.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Impaired working memory</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Working memory impairment belongs to the cognitive symptom cluster — the third category in the three-cluster framework, distinct from negative symptoms.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Affective flattening is a negative symptom. Remember the three-cluster framework: positive symptoms (delusions, hallucinations), negative symptoms (the 5 As), and cognitive symptoms (memory, attention, executive function)."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. Negative symptoms reflect a loss of normal functions and include the 5 As: avolition, alogia, anhedonia, affective flattening, and asociality."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
